Rosalind, Nathaniel,<br />
<br />
Vasseur-Kyle's letter of June 2 gives us everything we asked for on Item 4,=
 including the forward-looking commitment and the no-expiration language. R=
ecommend we close 2011-0447 on the undertaking.<br />
<br />
Two things I want on the record in EXAMTRAC.<br />
<br />
First, the disposition code should be C-4, closed on registrant undertaking=
, and not C-2, closed no further action. The difference matters. C-4 is wha=
t tells the next examiner that something was promised here and that verifyi=
ng it is part of the next exam's scope. C-2 tells them the staff found thin=
gs and decided none of them needed following up. That is not the same recor=
d and it is not the same next examination.<br />
<br />
Second, I am adding a follow-up flag on the account so the undertaking is p=
icked up in the risk scoring for the next cycle. The point of the open-ende=
d language is that it survives the people who negotiated it.<br />
<br />
Desmond